Z||000000||Mattsfiero||07-17-2001||09:48 AM||||Just curious is the 14" rims a different offset on a 88 grand am to the 14" fiero rims?<P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@aol.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||07-17-2001||10:03 AM||||The "Tech" 14" aluminum Wheels that were on Fiero's, Grand Am's and Sunbirds in the 80's are all the same offset and width. (6")||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mattsfiero||07-17-2001||10:09 AM||||Awsome thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-17-2001||10:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>The "Tech" 14" aluminum Wheels that were on Fiero's, Grand Am's and Sunbirds in the 80's are all the same offset and width. (6")</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Begging to differ... <BR>Grand Ams and Sunbirds may be the same. Fiero has about 1/2" less offset. Deeper dish when viewed from the front. The Fiero wheel has about 1/2" lip. The Grand Am and Sunbird rims are nearly flush with the front face of the hub. Has no lip to speak of.<BR>All are 6".<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tweek||07-17-2001||11:16 AM||||1988 Grand Am wheel:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.aaarims.com/wheels/1368.JPG"> <P><BR>1985 Fiero wheel:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.aaarims.com/wheels/1370.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||07-17-2001||12:25 PM||||I'll bet the GA's are 47mm offset vs the Fiero 35mm. The wheel will be in 12mm more. <P>I have the GA 16" 47mm offset wheels on my SC Fiero with no problems (stock suspension). I'm using 225/50-16's.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-17-2001||12:26 PM||||Just look on the back of the wheel..<P>14x6Jx35 14", 6" width, 35mm offset<P>16x6Jx47 16", 6" width, 47mm offset. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||sqoach||07-17-2001||12:56 PM||||Yep, definately different. There's a G/A wheel on my 86 SE. Didn't really notice it till I checked the brakes and saw that all the other ones stuck out a bit more. And that there's not much of a "lip" on it.<P>Almost forgot. If the G/A wheels have wheel weights on the inside, they will rub against the strut assembly. Noticed this when I took the wheel off the back. I swapped it to the front for the time being.<P><BR>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">       <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
